A synced password change checks the saved password and writes the new one in a single step, inside the password
store (#4707). `PasswordStoreInterface` gains `UpdateLoginsIfPasswordIs` and `AddLoginIfAbsent`. The built-in
backend runs each on the login database's own sequence, in one `sql::Transaction`.
- `UpdateLoginsIfPasswordIs`: every form must still be stored, under its primary key, with the expected password;
  otherwise nothing is written.
- `AddLoginIfAbsent`: adds the form only while no login (blocked and federated entries aside) for its signon
  realm and username is stored.
Either answers false and writes nothing when the check fails. Before this, `ac_passwords_replace` read the logins,
compared, then queued `UpdateLogins` or `AddLogin`, so an edit landing in between was overwritten (`UpdateLogins`
matches the row by key; `AddLogin` falls back to `INSERT OR REPLACE`). Other backends keep the default, which
answers false. Used only by `chrome/browser/ardia/ac_passwords_replace.cc`.

